        "text_Cw4Q3b": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Mark knows that food is medicine, and this Nobu-Style Miso-Glazed King Salmon is one of his go-to recipes for putting that philosophy into practice. </p><p>Our King Salmon is marinated for 48 hours in saké, miso, and coconut sugar until it turns deeply caramelized, then broiled and built into a bento box with sushi rice, blanched broccolini, pickled red onions, avocado, and salmon roe. A complete, nutrient-dense meal that holds up beautifully whether served warm or at room temperature. </p><p>It's the kind of dish that makes Mark's meal-prep rhythm effortless: marinate once, and you've got a week of restaurant-quality, omega-3-rich lunches and dinners ready to go.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
